{"Title":"An Act relative to providing fairness and equity in the retirement benefits of employees of the Massachusetts Water Resources Authority, sewer departments, sewer districts, water and sewer departments and districts, and wastewater facilities","BillNumber":"S1625","DocketNumber":"SD1401","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"N_C0","Name":"Nick Collins","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/N_C0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T14:24:18.193"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"N_C0","Name":"Nick Collins","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/N_C0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T14:24:18.1933333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1625/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Collins, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1625) of Nick Collins for legislation relative to providing fairness and equity in the retirement benefits of employees of the Massachusetts Water Resources Authority, sewer departments, sewer districts, water and sewer departments and districts, and wastewater facilities.  Public Service.","DocumentText":"\tSection (2)(g) of Chapter 32 of the Massachusetts General Laws is hereby amended by inserting after the word \"hospital,\" in line 256, the following words:-\r\n\t\"Operation and maintenance employees of water departments, water districts, sewer departments, sewer districts, water and sewer departments, water and sewer districts, and wastewater facilities, as well as operation and maintenance employees of the Massachusetts Water Resources Authority.\"\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}